 initial temperature was $-{1.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ After several minutes, the temperature of the liquid increased by ${7.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, at which point he decided to end the experiment. What was the final temperature of the liquid?" :question/worked-solution "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-{1.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{7.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={6.1}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was ${6.1}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096679 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3c9e3ef7-2d6f-526e-9ceb-fb21040b639e" :knowledge-point/title "Combining Operations on Negative Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0233853c-7d57-5992-a3de-9375ae31e3e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{2.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530866} {:answer/id #uuid "11599972-180e-564a-8500-e2e61a9c6541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530894} {:answer/id #uuid "11d8cfac-231b-5b5e-a776-de1a254087fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{5.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530897} {:answer/id #uuid "565ce699-4384-5be5-a535-10eb3fabc2a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{5.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531053} {:answer/id #uuid "64fa1bca-1096-5716-a7aa-e09d16681a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{3.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11599972-180e-564a-8500-e2e61a9c6541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530894} :answer-field/id #uuid "89a90e23-11a2-5c55-80c6-c90a2ec355b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aab3a1fe-f42d-5861-9d8c-8da472abefec" :question/math-academy-id "q-68925" :question/problem "In Toronto, Canada, the average temperature in November is ${4.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ In December, the average temperature decreases by ${5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November. Finally, in January, the average temperature decreases by ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to the previous month. Determine the average temperature in Toronto in January." :question/worked-solution "First, we must determine the average temperature in Toronto during the month of December. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in November. This gives\n\n$$\n{4.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{5.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{0.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature during the month of January. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to December, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in December. This gives\n\n$$\n-{0.5}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{3.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Toronto in January is $-{3.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c37cc3b9-6255-5fb6-bb61-6cae10cd9531" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 